{
  "_readme": [
    "Curated Bay Area annual events. These are the things locals plan around and",
    "that no scraper reliably surfaces months ahead - the scraped sources only",
    "know about next week.",
    "",
    "Dates are RULES, not fixed dates, so this file does not rot every January.",
    "Rule types (weekday: 0=Monday .. 6=Sunday, matching Python's weekday()):",
    "  fixed              {month, day}",
    "  nth_weekday        {month, weekday, n}         n=1..5, or n=-1 for last",
    "  nth_weekend        {month, n, span_days}       n-th Saturday, span_days long",
    "  last_full_weekend  {month, span_days}          last Sat+Sun wholly in month",
    "  after_nth_weekday  {month, weekday, n, offset_days}",
    "  monthly_nth_weekday{weekday, n}                every month",
    "",
    "'approx' true means the timing is typical-but-unconfirmed for the year -",
    "the UI flags these. 'notability' (0-100) is a popularity prior: roughly how",
    "many people organize their weekend around it. It seeds the ranker; it is",
    "not attendance."
  ],
